 <div class="section"><h2>About Shimla</h2><p class="desc">Shimla, the state capital, served as the summer capital of British India from 1864. The district blends Victorian architecture — the Viceregal Lodge, Christ Church, Gaiety Theatre — with dense cedar and rhododendron forests. Beyond the city, Shimla district offers Narkanda for skiing, Rampur for tribal culture, Chail for the world's highest cricket ground, and Rohru for off-the-beaten-path apple orchards.</p></div>
 <div class="section" id="facts"><h2>Quick Facts</h2><div class="facts-grid"><div class="fact-card"><div class="label">District HQ</div><div class="value">Shimla</div></div><div class="fact-card"><div class="label">Area</div><div class="value">5131 km²</div></div><div class="fact-card"><div class="label">Altitude</div><div class="value">300–3700 m</div></div><div class="fact-card"><div class="label">Best Season</div><div class="value">Mar–Jun, Sep–Nov, Dec–Feb (snow)</div></div><div class="fact-card"><div class="label">Summer Temp</div><div class="value">15–30°C</div></div><div class="fact-card"><div class="label">Winter Temp</div><div class="value">-5–10°C</div></div><div class="fact-card"><div class="label">Nearest Airport</div><div class="value">Shimla Airport (Jubbarhatti)</div></div><div class="fact-card"><div class="label">From Delhi</div><div class="value">343 km</div></div></div></div>
-<div class="section" id="places"><h2>Top Places to Visit (23)</h2><div class="places-grid"><div class="place-card"><h3>The Ridge & Mall Road</h3><div class="place-tag-row"><span>2,213 m</span><span>Shimla town centre</span></div><ul class="place-facts"><li>Ceremonial and social heart of British Shimla, summer capital of India from 1864 to 1939</li><li>Christ Church (1857), one of the oldest churches in northern India, anchors the eastern end</li><li>Gaiety Theatre (1887) on Mall Road still hosts live performances</li><li>Traffic-free promenade with panoramic views of the Shivalik and Dhauladhar ranges</li></ul><button type="button" class="place-map-btn" onclick="toggleMapBox(this)">🧭 View on Map</button><div class="map-box" style="display:none;margin-top:10px"><iframe width="100%" height="200" style="border:0;border-radius:8px;display:block" loading="lazy" referrerpolicy="no-referrer-when-downgrade" data-src="https://maps.google.com/maps?q=31.1048,77.1734&z=15&output=embed"></iframe><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&destination=31.1048,77.1734" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="map-link">Open in Google Maps →</a></div></div><div class="place-card"><h3>Jakhu Temple</h3><div class="place-tag-row"><span>2,455 m</span><span>2 km trek from the Ridge</span></div><ul class="place-facts"><li>Highest point of the Shimla ridge; one of Himachal's most visited Hanuman temples</li><li>Forest trail home to a large, bold population of rhesus monkeys</li><li>Ropeway (gondola) links the Ridge to the hilltop</li><li>33-metre Hanuman statue installed in 2010, visible across central Shimla</li></ul><button type="button" class="place-map-btn" onclick="toggleMapBox(this)">🧭 View on Map</button><div class="map-box" style="display:none;margin-top:10px"><iframe width="100%" height="200" style="border:0;border-radius:8px;display:block" loading="lazy" referrerpolicy="no-referrer-when-downgrade" data-src="https://maps.google.com/maps?q=31.1099,77.1813&z=15&output=embed"></iframe><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&destination=31.1099,77.1813" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="map-link">Open in Google Maps →</a></div></div><div class="place-card"><h3>Viceregal Lodge</h3><div class="place-tag-row"><span>Observatory Hill</span><span>Completed 1888</span></div><ul class="place-facts"><li>Former official summer residence of the British Viceroy; now Indian Institute of Advanced Study</li><li>Scottish baronial architecture in grey limestone, with terraced gardens</li><li>Hosted the Shimla Conference of 1945, which shaped the Partition of India</li><li>Guided tours through the state rooms, library and Viceregal office</li></ul><button type="button" class="place-map-btn" onclick="toggleMapBox(this)">🧭 View on Map</button><div class="map-box" style="display:none;margin-top:10px"><iframe width="100%" height="200" style="border:0;border-radius:8px;display:block" loading="lazy" referrerpolicy="no-referrer-when-downgrade" data-src="https://maps.google.com/maps?q=31.1003,77.1652&z=15&output=embed"></iframe><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&destination=31.1003,77.1652" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="map-link">Open in Google Maps →</a></div></div><div class="place-card"><h3>Kufri</h3><div class="place-tag-row"><span>2,622 m</span><span>16 km from Shimla</span></div><ul class="place-facts"><li>Most accessible skiing and snow-play spot from the state capital, Dec–Feb</li><li>Himalayan Nature Park: snow leopards, Himalayan brown bears, pheasants</li><li>Summer base for yak rides and walks to Mahasu Peak (2,850 m)</li><li>Drive passes through apple orchards, best in late September</li></ul><button type="button" class="place-map-btn" onclick="toggleMapBox(this)">🧭 View on Map</button><div class="map-box" style="display:none;margin-top:10px"><iframe width="100%" height="200" style="border:0;border-radius:8px;display:block" loading="lazy" referrerpolicy="no-referrer-when-downgrade" data-src="https://maps.google.com/maps?q=31.0962,77.2673&z=15&output=embed"></iframe><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&destination=31.0962,77.2673" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="map-link">Open in Google Maps →</a></div></div><div class="place-card"><h3>Narkanda</h3><div class="place-tag-row"><span>2,708 m</span><span>Old Hindustan-Tibet Road</span></div><ul class="place-facts"><li>One of Shimla district's highest towns and a major apple-growing belt</li><li>Orchards bloom white in May; harvest crates line the roads Aug–Oct</li><li>Government ski slopes on Hatu ridge, open January–March</li><li>Hatu Peak temple (3,400 m) a 7 km drive away</li></ul><button type="button" class="place-map-btn" onclick="toggleMapBox(this)">🧭 View on Map</button><div class="map-box" style="display:none;margin-top:10px"><iframe width="100%" height="200" style="border:0;border-radius:8px;display:block" loading="lazy" referrerpolicy="no-referrer-when-downgrade" data-src="https://maps.google.com/maps?q=31.2741,77.4554&z=15&output=embed"></iframe><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&destination=31.2741,77.4554" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="map-link">Open in Google Maps →</a></div></div><div class="place-card"><h3>Chail</h3><div class="place-tag-row"><span>2,250 m</span><span>Solan / Shimla border</span></div><ul class="place-facts"><li>Created in 1891 by Maharaja Bhupinder Singh of Patiala</li><li>Chail Palace, now a heritage hotel run by Himachal Tourism</li><li>Chail Cricket Ground (1893) — Guinness-certified as the world's highest cricket ground</li><li>Forest sanctuary with pheasants, barking deer and leopard</li></ul><button type="button" class="place-map-btn" onclick="toggleMapBox(this)">🧭 View on Map</button><div class="map-box" style="display:none;margin-top:10px"><iframe width="100%" height="200" style="border:0;border-radius:8px;display:block" loading="lazy" referrerpolicy="no-referrer-when-downgrade" data-src="https://maps.google.com/maps?q=30.9694,77.2014&z=15&output=embed"></iframe><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&destination=30.9694,77.2014" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="map-link">Open in Google Maps →</a></div></div><div class="place-card"><h3>Rampur</h3><div class="place-tag-row"><span>1,000 m</span><span>On the Satluj river</span></div><ul class="place-facts"><li>Historic trading post on the old Tibet road, known as Rampur Bushahr</li><li>Annual Lavi Fair (November), running for 300+ years</li><li>Padam Palace blends Mughal, Tibetan and European architecture</li><li>Gateway town to Kinnaur</li></ul><button type="button" class="place-map-btn" onclick="toggleMapBox(this)">🧭 View on Map</button><div class="map-box" style="display:none;margin-top:10px"><iframe width="100%" height="200" style="border:0;border-radius:8px;display:block" loading="lazy" referrerpolicy="no-referrer-when-downgrade" data-src="https://maps.google.com/maps?q=31.4484,77.6316&z=15&output=embed"></iframe><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&destination=31.4484,77.6316" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="map-link">Open in Google Maps →</a></div></div><div class="place-card"><h3>Rohru</h3><div class="place-tag-row"><span>1,525 m</span><span>On the Pabbar river</span></div><ul class="place-facts"><li>Premium apple-growing valley, far less touristed than central Shimla</li><li>Pabbar river is a recognised brown trout fishery (permit system)</li><li>Chirgaon (30 km) is base for winter walks and the Chanshal Pass route (4,520 m, opens June)</li><li>Among the most offbeat valley experiences in the district</li></ul><button type="button" class="place-map-btn" onclick="toggleMapBox(this)">🧭 View on Map</button><div class="map-box" style="display:none;margin-top:10px"><iframe width="100%" height="200" style="border:0;border-radius:8px;display:block" loading="lazy" referrerpolicy="no-referrer-when-downgrade" data-src="https://maps.google.com/maps?q=31.1996,77.7497&z=15&output=embed"></iframe><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&destination=31.1996,77.7497" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="map-link">Open in Google Maps →</a></div></div><div class="place-card"><h3>Tattapani</h3><div class="place-tag-row"><span>River-level</span><span>On the Satluj</span></div><ul class="place-facts"><li>Natural sulphur hot springs — the name means 'hot water'</li><li>Springs now partially submerged by the Koldam dam reservoir</li><li>River rafting on the Tattapani–Sunni stretch (14 km), Oct–Apr</li><li>Warmer microclimate makes it a popular winter escape from Shimla</li></ul><button type="button" class="place-map-btn" onclick="toggleMapBox(this)">🧭 View on Map</button><div class="map-box" style="display:none;margin-top:10px"><iframe width="100%" height="200" style="border:0;border-radius:8px;display:block" loading="lazy" referrerpolicy="no-referrer-when-downgrade" data-src="https://maps.google.com/maps?q=31.3297,77.1123&z=15&output=embed"></iframe><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&destination=31.3297,77.1123" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="map-link">Open in Google Maps →</a></div></div><div class="place-card"><h3>Hatu Peak</h3><div class="place-tag-row"><span>3,400 m</span><span>Near Narkanda</span></div><ul class="place-facts"><li>Highest point in the Narkanda area, reached by paved road through fir and deodar forest</li><li>Ancient Hatu Mata temple stands at the summit</li><li>360° views: Kinnaur Kailash, Dhauladhar and Spiti peaks</li><li>Popular pre-dawn drive for sunrise viewing</li></ul><button type="button" class="place-map-btn" onclick="toggleMapBox(this)">🧭 View on Map</button><div class="map-box" style="display:none;margin-top:10px"><iframe width="100%" height="200" style="border:0;border-radius:8px;display:block" loading="lazy" referrerpolicy="no-referrer-when-downgrade" data-src="https://maps.google.com/maps?q=31.2614,77.4372&z=15&output=embed"></iframe><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&destination=31.2614,77.4372" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="map-link">Open in Google Maps →</a></div></div><div class="place-card"><h3>Glen</h3><div class="place-tag-row"><span>1,830 m</span><span>4 km from the Ridge</span></div><ul class="place-facts"><li>Quiet forested hollow with a small stream through deodar cover</li><li>Easy, shaded walk down from Mall Road</li><li>Passes the old Cecil Hotel and Kennedy House</li><li>Popular half-day picnic spot, quieter by afternoon</li></ul><button type="button" class="place-map-btn" onclick="toggleMapBox(this)">🧭 View on Map</button><div class="map-box" style="display:none;margin-top:10px"><iframe width="100%" height="200" style="border:0;border-radius:8px;display:block" loading="lazy" referrerpolicy="no-referrer-when-downgrade" data-src="https://maps.google.com/maps?q=31.1177,77.1546&z=15&output=embed"></iframe><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&destination=31.1177,77.1546" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="map-link">Open in Google Maps →</a></div></div><div class="place-card"><h3>Summer Hill</h3><div class="place-tag-row"><span>2,123 m</span><span>5 km from the Ridge</span></div><ul class="place-facts"><li>One of Shimla's original residential suburbs, on a gentler slope</li><li>Home to Himachal Pradesh University</li><li>Quiet lanes between old colonial bungalows and campus housing</li><li>Cafés cater to a student crowd rather than tour groups</li></ul><button type="button" class="place-map-btn" onclick="toggleMapBox(this)">🧭 View on Map</button><div class="map-box" style="display:none;margin-top:10px"><iframe width="100%" height="200" style="border:0;border-radius:8px;display:block" loading="lazy" referrerpolicy="no-referrer-when-downgrade" data-src="https://maps.google.com/maps?q=31.1076,77.1489&z=15&output=embed"></iframe><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&destination=31.1076,77.1489" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="map-link">Open in Google Maps →</a></div></div><div class="place-card"><h3>Kamna Devi (Prospect Hill)</h3><div class="place-tag-row"><span>2,145 m</span><span>5 km from the Ridge</span></div><ul class="place-facts"><li>Kamna Devi temple crowns the summit near Boileauganj</li><li>Panoramic view of Shimla town, Jutogh, Summer Hill and Tara Devi</li><li>Best light in the last hour before sunset</li><li>A quieter alternative to the busier Jakhu Hill</li></ul><button type="button" class="place-map-btn" onclick="toggleMapBox(this)">🧭 View on Map</button><div class="map-box" style="display:none;margin-top:10px"><iframe width="100%" height="200" style="border:0;border-radius:8px;display:block" loading="lazy" referrerpolicy="no-referrer-when-downgrade" data-src="https://maps.google.com/maps?q=31.0968,77.1476&z=15&output=embed"></iframe><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&destination=31.0968,77.1476" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="map-link">Open in Google Maps →</a></div></div><div class="place-card"><h3>Wild Flower Hall</h3><div class="place-tag-row"><span>Forested hillside</span><span>13 km from Shimla</span></div><ul class="place-facts"><li>Former residence of the Commander-in-Chief of British India</li><li>Rebuilt as a luxury hotel after a major fire destroyed the original</li><li>Nearby: Lord Curzon's 'Retreat' and 'Hem Kunj', former Punjab Governor's resort</li><li>Set within dense pine forest with views toward the snow line</li></ul><button type="button" class="place-map-btn" onclick="toggleMapBox(this)">🧭 View on Map</button><div class="map-box" style="display:none;margin-top:10px"><iframe width="100%" height="200" style="border:0;border-radius:8px;display:block" loading="lazy" referrerpolicy="no-referrer-when-downgrade" data-src="https://maps.google.com/maps?q=31.1372,77.2264&z=15&output=embed"></iframe><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&destination=31.1372,77.2264" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="map-link">Open in Google Maps →</a></div></div><div class="place-card"><h3>Tara Devi</h3><div class="place-tag-row"><span>2,100 m</span><span>8 km from Shimla</span></div><ul class="place-facts"><li>Hilltop temple reached by a short climb through pine forest</li><li>Calmer alternative to the busier Ridge-area temples</li><li>Views over the valley toward Kasumpti</li><li>Shimla's railway line visible winding below</li></ul><button type="button" class="place-map-btn" onclick="toggleMapBox(this)">🧭 View on Map</button><div class="map-box" style="display:none;margin-top:10px"><iframe width="100%" height="200" style="border:0;border-radius:8px;display:block" loading="lazy" referrerpolicy="no-referrer-when-downgrade" data-src="https://maps.google.com/maps?q=31.0654,77.1252&z=15&output=embed"></iframe><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&destination=31.0654,77.1252" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="map-link">Open in Google Maps →</a></div></div><div class="place-card"><h3>Mashobra</h3><div class="place-tag-row"><span>2,149 m</span><span>13 km from Shimla</span></div><ul class="place-facts"><li>Old forest town with apple orchards and quiet walking trails</li><li>Hosts the annual Sipi Fair every June</li><li>Coutts' Garden: planted 1887, 100+ English apple varieties</li><li>Rainwater-harvesting tanks from 1889 still functional</li><li>Now part of the Fruit Research Centre under Dr YS Parmar Horticulture University</li></ul><button type="button" class="place-map-btn" onclick="toggleMapBox(this)">🧭 View on Map</button><div class="map-box" style="display:none;margin-top:10px"><iframe width="100%" height="200" style="border:0;border-radius:8px;display:block" loading="lazy" referrerpolicy="no-referrer-when-downgrade" data-src="https://maps.google.com/maps?q=31.1372,77.2264&z=15&output=embed"></iframe><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&destination=31.1372,77.2264" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="map-link">Open in Google Maps →</a></div></div><div class="place-card"><h3>Naldera</h3><div class="place-tag-row"><span>3,044 m</span><span>22 km from Shimla</span></div><ul class="place-facts"><li>One of India's oldest golf courses (nine holes), laid out by Lord Curzon in 1903</li><li>Broad grassy plateau ringed by deodar forest</li><li>Surrounding villages hold temples in distinctive hill architecture</li><li>Popular half-day trip from Shimla</li></ul><button type="button" class="place-map-btn" onclick="toggleMapBox(this)">🧭 View on Map</button><div class="map-box" style="display:none;margin-top:10px"><iframe width="100%" height="200" style="border:0;border-radius:8px;display:block" loading="lazy" referrerpolicy="no-referrer-when-downgrade" data-src="https://maps.google.com/maps?q=31.1642,77.2528&z=15&output=embed"></iframe><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&destination=31.1642,77.2528" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="map-link">Open in Google Maps →</a></div></div><div class="place-card"><h3>Fagu</h3><div class="place-tag-row"><span>2,510 m</span><span>22 km from Shimla</span></div><ul class="place-facts"><li>Small, quiet hamlet surrounded by apple orchards</li><li>Recognised trekking stage toward Shali Peak and Churdhar</li><li>Sweeping Himalayan views, far less developed than Kufri or Narkanda</li></ul><button type="button" class="place-map-btn" onclick="toggleMapBox(this)">🧭 View on Map</button><div class="map-box" style="display:none;margin-top:10px"><iframe width="100%" height="200" style="border:0;border-radius:8px;display:block" loading="lazy" referrerpolicy="no-referrer-when-downgrade" data-src="https://maps.google.com/maps?q=31.1421,77.2843&z=15&output=embed"></iframe><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&destination=31.1421,77.2843" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="map-link">Open in Google Maps →</a></div></div><div class="place-card"><h3>State Museum, Shimla</h3><div class="place-tag-row"><span>Colonial mansion</span><span>Near Mall Road</span></div><ul class="place-facts"><li>Stone sculptures: Varuna (Masrur), Vishnu (Nirmand), Vishnu-Lakshmi on Garuda (Mandi)</li><li>Three-faced Shiva and Simha Vahini Durga, both originally from Kullu</li><li>Kangra school miniature paintings and Chamba wall paintings</li><li>Galleries for arms, coins (Tankri/Nagari scripts), Gandhi, Pahari dolls and philately</li></ul><button type="button" class="place-map-btn" onclick="toggleMapBox(this)">🧭 View on Map</button><div class="map-box" style="display:none;margin-top:10px"><iframe width="100%" height="200" style="border:0;border-radius:8px;display:block" loading="lazy" referrerpolicy="no-referrer-when-downgrade" data-src="https://maps.google.com/maps?q=31.0928,77.1636&z=15&output=embed"></iframe><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&destination=31.0928,77.1636" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="map-link">Open in Google Maps →</a></div></div><div class="place-card"><h3>Gorton Castle</h3><div class="place-tag-row"><span>Mid-19th century</span><span>Shimla town</span></div><ul class="place-facts"><li>Named for an Indian Civil Service officer; later owned by banker Sir James Walker</li><li>Neo-Gothic redesign by Sir Samuel Swinton Jacob, with Rajasthani-style stone jaalis</li><li>Housed colonial government departments from 1905</li><li>Now the office of the Accountant-General of Himachal Pradesh</li><li>Top two storeys destroyed in a fire, January 2014</li></ul><button type="button" class="place-map-btn" onclick="toggleMapBox(this)">🧭 View on Map</button><div class="map-box" style="display:none;margin-top:10px"><iframe width="100%" height="200" style="border:0;border-radius:8px;display:block" loading="lazy" referrerpolicy="no-referrer-when-downgrade" data-src="https://maps.google.com/maps?q=31.1012,77.1789&z=15&output=embed"></iframe><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&destination=31.1012,77.1789" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="map-link">Open in Google Maps →</a></div></div><div class="place-card"><h3>Junga</h3><div class="place-tag-row"><span>~26 km from Shimla</span></div><ul class="place-facts"><li>Former capital of the princely state of Keonthal, founded 1211 AD by Giri Sen</li><li>Old wooden Junga Palace, 300+ years old, built by Raja Sansar Sen</li><li>Newer 19th-century palace built nearby at Chowri</li><li>Keonthal state merged into Himachal Pradesh after independence</li><li>Quiet destination known for temples, orchards and birdlife</li></ul><button type="button" class="place-map-btn" onclick="toggleMapBox(this)">🧭 View on Map</button><div class="map-box" style="display:none;margin-top:10px"><iframe width="100%" height="200" style="border:0;border-radius:8px;display:block" loading="lazy" referrerpolicy="no-referrer-when-downgrade" data-src="https://maps.google.com/maps?q=31.0167,77.2667&z=15&output=embed"></iframe><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&destination=31.0167,77.2667" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="map-link">Open in Google Maps →</a></div></div><div class="place-card"><h3>Hatkoti (Pabbar Valley)</h3><div class="place-tag-row"><span>95 km from Shimla</span><span>Pabbar Valley</span></div><ul class="place-facts"><li>Known as the 'valley of temples' for its density of ancient shrines</li><li>Durga and Shiva temples in Shikhara style, from three historical periods</li><li>Legendary founding attributed to Shankaracharya; reroofed under Raja Padam Chandra of Jubbal</li><li>Rare bronze Mahishasurmardini Durga image; torna with a 9th-century inscription</li><li>Protected by the Archaeological Survey of India</li><li>Pabbar river here is a recognised trout fishery</li></ul><button type="button" class="place-map-btn" onclick="toggleMapBox(this)">🧭 View on Map</button><div class="map-box" style="display:none;margin-top:10px"><iframe width="100%" height="200" style="border:0;border-radius:8px;display:block" loading="lazy" referrerpolicy="no-referrer-when-downgrade" data-src="https://maps.google.com/maps?q=31.3230,77.5940&z=15&output=embed"></iframe><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&destination=31.3230,77.5940" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="map-link">Open in Google Maps →</a></div></div><div class="place-card"><h3>Sarahan</h3><div class="place-tag-row"><span>2,165 m</span><span>~174 km from Shimla</span></div><ul class="place-facts"><li>Home to the Bhimakali Temple, a fusion of Hindu and Buddhist architecture</li><li>Gateway town to Kinnaur</li><li>Sports Authority of India's High Altitude Training Centre located here</li><li>Views toward the Srikhand range and Sutlej valley</li></ul><button type="button" class="place-map-btn" onclick="toggleMapBox(this)">🧭 View on Map</button><div class="map-box" style="display:none;margin-top:10px"><iframe width="100%" height="200" style="border:0;border-radius:8px;display:block" loading="lazy" referrerpolicy="no-referrer-when-downgrade" data-src="https://maps.google.com/maps?q=31.5167,77.7833&z=15&output=embed"></iframe><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&destination=31.5167,77.7833" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="map-link">Open in Google Maps →</a></div></div></div></div>
+<div class="section" id="places"><h2>Top Places to Visit (23)</h2><div class="places-grid"><div class="place-card"><h3>The Ridge & Mall Road</h3><div class="place-tag-row"><span>2,213 m</span><span>Shimla town centre</span></div><ul class="place-facts"><li>Ceremonial and social heart of British Shimla, summer capital of India from 1864 to 1939</li><li>Christ Church (1857), one of the oldest churches in northern India, anchors the eastern end</li><li>Gaiety Theatre (1887) on Mall Road still hosts live performances</li><li>Traffic-free promenade with panoramic views of the Shivalik and Dhauladhar ranges</li></ul><button type="button" class="place-map-btn" onclick="toggleMapBox(this)">🧭 View on Map</button><div class="map-box" style="display:none;margin-top:10px"><iframe width="100%" height="200" style="border:0;border-radius:8px;display:block" loading="lazy" referrerpolicy="no-referrer-when-downgrade" data-src="https://maps.google.com/maps?q=31.1048,77.1734&z=15&output=embed"></iframe><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&destination=31.1048,77.1734" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="map-link">Open in Google Maps →</a></div></div><div class="place-card"><img src="https://drive.google.com/thumbnail?id=1Ipwl5Th_AufIWSNr5qGjiXoG_ddYdQpi&sz=w600" alt="Jakhu Temple" loading="lazy"><h3>Jakhu Temple</h3><div class="place-tag-row"><span>2,455 m</span><span>2 km trek from the Ridge</span></div><ul class="place-facts"><li>Highest point of the Shimla ridge; one of Himachal's most visited Hanuman temples</li><li>Forest trail home to a large, bold population of rhesus monkeys</li><li>Ropeway (gondola) links the Ridge to the hilltop</li><li>33-metre Hanuman statue installed in 2010, visible across central Shimla</li></ul><button type="button" class="place-map-btn" onclick="toggleMapBox(this)">🧭 View on Map</button><div class="map-box" style="display:none;margin-top:10px"><iframe width="100%" height="200" style="border:0;border-radius:8px;display:block" loading="lazy" referrerpolicy="no-referrer-when-downgrade" data-src="https://maps.google.com/maps?q=31.1099,77.1813&z=15&output=embed"></iframe><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&destination=31.1099,77.1813" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="map-link">Open in Google Maps →</a></div></div><div class="place-card"><h3>Viceregal Lodge</h3><div class="place-tag-row"><span>Observatory Hill</span><span>Completed 1888</span></div><ul class="place-facts"><li>Former official summer residence of the British Viceroy; now Indian Institute of Advanced Study</li><li>Scottish baronial architecture in grey limestone, with terraced gardens</li><li>Hosted the Shimla Conference of 1945, which shaped the Partition of India</li><li>Guided tours through the state rooms, library and Viceregal office</li></ul><button type="button" class="place-map-btn" onclick="toggleMapBox(this)">🧭 View on Map</button><div class="map-box" style="display:none;margin-top:10px"><iframe width="100%" height="200" style="border:0;border-radius:8px;display:block" loading="lazy" referrerpolicy="no-referrer-when-downgrade" data-src="https://maps.google.com/maps?q=31.1003,77.1652&z=15&output=embed"></iframe><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&destination=31.1003,77.1652" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="map-link">Open in Google Maps →</a></div></div><div class="place-card"><img src="https://drive.google.com/thumbnail?id=1w24nJuzPjXjJ_mOysEZlcJUrbYjuoBqZ&sz=w600" alt="Kufri" loading="lazy"><h3>Kufri</h3><div class="place-tag-row"><span>2,622 m</span><span>16 km from Shimla</span></div><ul class="place-facts"><li>Most accessible skiing and snow-play spot from the state capital, Dec–Feb</li><li>Himalayan Nature Park: snow leopards, Himalayan brown bears, pheasants</li><li>Summer base for yak rides and walks to Mahasu Peak (2,850 m)</li><li>Drive passes through apple orchards, best in late September</li></ul><button type="button" class="place-map-btn" onclick="toggleMapBox(this)">🧭 View on Map</button><div class="map-box" style="display:none;margin-top:10px"><iframe width="100%" height="200" style="border:0;border-radius:8px;display:block" loading="lazy" referrerpolicy="no-referrer-when-downgrade" data-src="https://maps.google.com/maps?q=31.0962,77.2673&z=15&output=embed"></iframe><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&destination=31.0962,77.2673" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="map-link">Open in Google Maps →</a></div></div><div class="place-card"><img src="https://drive.google.com/thumbnail?id=1zyML626vzyNAfQaMMYLr1lsIBCBjUvqQ&sz=w600" alt="Narkanda" loading="lazy"><h3>Narkanda</h3><div class="place-tag-row"><span>2,708 m</span><span>Old Hindustan-Tibet Road</span></div><ul class="place-facts"><li>One of Shimla district's highest towns and a major apple-growing belt</li><li>Orchards bloom white in May; harvest crates line the roads Aug–Oct</li><li>Government ski slopes on Hatu ridge, open January–March</li><li>Hatu Peak temple (3,400 m) a 7 km drive away</li></ul><button type="button" class="place-map-btn" onclick="toggleMapBox(this)">🧭 View on Map</button><div class="map-box" style="display:none;margin-top:10px"><iframe width="100%" height="200" style="border:0;border-radius:8px;display:block" loading="lazy" referrerpolicy="no-referrer-when-downgrade" data-src="https://maps.google.com/maps?q=31.2741,77.4554&z=15&output=embed"></iframe><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&destination=31.2741,77.4554" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="map-link">Open in Google Maps →</a></div></div><div class="place-card"><h3>Chail</h3><div class="place-tag-row"><span>2,250 m</span><span>Solan / Shimla border</span></div><ul class="place-facts"><li>Created in 1891 by Maharaja Bhupinder Singh of Patiala</li><li>Chail Palace, now a heritage hotel run by Himachal Tourism</li><li>Chail Cricket Ground (1893) — Guinness-certified as the world's highest cricket ground</li><li>Forest sanctuary with pheasants, barking deer and leopard</li></ul><button type="button" class="place-map-btn" onclick="toggleMapBox(this)">🧭 View on Map</button><div class="map-box" style="display:none;margin-top:10px"><iframe width="100%" height="200" style="border:0;border-radius:8px;display:block" loading="lazy" referrerpolicy="no-referrer-when-downgrade" data-src="https://maps.google.com/maps?q=30.9694,77.2014&z=15&output=embed"></iframe><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&destination=30.9694,77.2014" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="map-link">Open in Google Maps →</a></div></div><div class="place-card"><h3>Rampur</h3><div class="place-tag-row"><span>1,000 m</span><span>On the Satluj river</span></div><ul class="place-facts"><li>Historic trading post on the old Tibet road, known as Rampur Bushahr</li><li>Annual Lavi Fair (November), running for 300+ years</li><li>Padam Palace blends Mughal, Tibetan and European architecture</li><li>Gateway town to Kinnaur</li></ul><button type="button" class="place-map-btn" onclick="toggleMapBox(this)">🧭 View on Map</button><div class="map-box" style="display:none;margin-top:10px"><iframe width="100%" height="200" style="border:0;border-radius:8px;display:block" loading="lazy" referrerpolicy="no-referrer-when-downgrade" data-src="https://maps.google.com/maps?q=31.4484,77.6316&z=15&output=embed"></iframe><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&destination=31.4484,77.6316" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="map-link">Open in Google Maps →</a></div></div><div class="place-card"><h3>Rohru</h3><div class="place-tag-row"><span>1,525 m</span><span>On the Pabbar river</span></div><ul class="place-facts"><li>Premium apple-growing valley, far less touristed than central Shimla</li><li>Pabbar river is a recognised brown trout fishery (permit system)</li><li>Chirgaon (30 km) is base for winter walks and the Chanshal Pass route (4,520 m, opens June)</li><li>Among the most offbeat valley experiences in the district</li></ul><button type="button" class="place-map-btn" onclick="toggleMapBox(thi