ton" class="place-map-btn" onclick="toggleMapBox(this)">🧭 View on Map</button><div class="map-box" style="display:none;margin-top:10px"><iframe width="100%" height="200" style="border:0;border-radius:8px;display:block" loading="lazy" referrerpolicy="no-referrer-when-downgrade" data-src="https://maps.google.com/maps?q=31.1012,77.1789&z=15&output=embed"></iframe><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&destination=31.1012,77.1789" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="map-link">Open in Google Maps →</a></div></div><div class="place-card"><h3>Junga</h3><div class="place-tag-row"><span>~26 km from Shimla</span></div><ul class="place-facts"><li>Former capital of the princely state of Keonthal, founded 1211 AD by Giri Sen</li><li>Old wooden Junga Palace, 300+ years old, built by Raja Sansar Sen</li><li>Newer 19th-century palace built nearby at Chowri</li><li>Keonthal state merged into Himachal Pradesh after independence</li><li>Quiet destination known for temples, orchards and birdlife</li></ul><button type="button" class="place-map-btn" onclick="toggleMapBox(this)">🧭 View on Map</button><div class="map-box" style="display:none;margin-top:10px"><iframe width="100%" height="200" style="border:0;border-radius:8px;display:block" loading="lazy" referrerpolicy="no-referrer-when-downgrade" data-src="https://maps.google.com/maps?q=31.0167,77.2667&z=15&output=embed"></iframe><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&destination=31.0167,77.2667" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="map-link">Open in Google Maps →</a></div></div><div class="place-card"><h3>Hatkoti (Pabbar Valley)</h3><div class="place-tag-row"><span>95 km from Shimla</span><span>Pabbar Valley</span></div><ul class="place-facts"><li>Known as the 'valley of temples' for its density of ancient shrines</li><li>Durga and Shiva temples in Shikhara style, from three historical periods</li><li>Legendary founding attributed to Shankaracharya; reroofed under Raja Padam Chandra of Jubbal</li><li>Rare bronze Mahi